       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Requested:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Usual limits:** The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. Single doses are usually capped at 800 mg. This order is twice the daily maximum, and each dose is twice the usual single-dose limit.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the patient would face a high risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO three or four times daily**, which is the usual range.\n- **1600 mg per day in total**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf you really want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though it may still need pharmacist or prescriber review. Tell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
