       "text": "I won't enter ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for going past the safety limit. At 6,400 mg/day the patient would face a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Confirming the order doesn't lower that risk.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, or another dose you choose within the usual range.\n\nIf the patient's pain or inflammation isn't controlled at the maximum dose, you could add a different analgesic, such as scheduled acetaminophen, or consult pharmacy or the pain service. If you think this dose is clinically necessary, the prescriber should talk with pharmacy directly so the decision is documented and reviewed.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
